---
import Base from "../layouts/Base.astro";
import DemoExplorer from "../components/DemoExplorer.astro";
import demo from "../data/demo.json";

// A *recording*, not a live endpoint. The questions were run against the hub's
// indexes on the date the data carries, and the hits were committed. Live
// querying needs the API (component 16 §5's `/api/demo/query`), which arrives
// with step 4; until then a page that pretended to query would be lying about
// where its answers came from. `twin={null}`: twins are written for
// `src/content/**`, and the prose that belongs in the llms family is the essay
// this page links.
const title = "Semantic indexing, recorded";
const description =
  "The same questions run three ways against one indexed docset — keyword (BM25), vector, and the reciprocal-rank fusion of both — with the hits and the timings as they were recorded on " +
  demo.generated + ".";
const exact = demo.questions.filter((q) => q.kind === "exact-token").length;
const paraphrase = demo.questions.length - exact;
---
<Base title={title} description={description} route="/demo/" twin={null}>
  <p>
    An indexed docset can be asked a question two ways, and the two ways fail in
    opposite directions. Ask for <code>CLAUDE_CODE_SYNC_SKILLS</code> and BM25 has
    the literal string while the embedding of a lone identifier is a weak vector.
    Ask “which hook events fire once per turn” and the embedding knows what you
    mean while BM25 matches on <code>hook</code> and <code>events</code> everywhere.
    Below, {demo.questions.length} questions — {exact} exact-token probes and
    {paraphrase} paraphrases from the golden set — are run all three ways so the
    trade is visible rather than asserted.
  </p>

  <h2>This is a recording</h2>
  <p>
    Every hit and every timing on this page was <strong>recorded on {demo.generated}</strong>
    and committed as <code>src/data/demo.json</code>. The page runs no query: there
    is no backend behind it, and there will not be one until the API lands. What
    you are reading is what <code>{demo.docset}</code> answered that day —
    the <code>{demo.layer}</code> layer, {demo.top} hits per leg, embedded with
    <code>{demo.model}</code> against <code>{demo.embedPool}</code> on one laptop.
    Timings are one run on one machine: treat the <em>ratio</em> between the legs
    as the finding and the absolute milliseconds as weather. Bracketed
    <code>[tokens]</code> in a keyword snippet are FTS5 marking what it matched.
  </p>
  <p>
    To run the same questions against your own docset, see
    <a href="/reference/">the reference</a> for the commands, and
    <a href="/essays/semantic-indexing/">the essay</a> for what the two legs are
    doing and why the fusion is the default.
  </p>

  <h2>The three legs</h2>
  <DemoExplorer data={demo} />
</Base>
